      "side": 1,
      "message": "It might be useful to look at one of the voltha components (for example the voltha-go repository) to see how we do it there. What we do is have a Makefile target (`make mod-update`) that updates the go.mod/go.sum files and runs `go mod vendor`. The vendor directory then gets check in to the repository.That way, the repository always has a complete copy of the dependencies, and we can never be in a situation where a third party removes a dependency, breaking our build.",
